# Copy to .env for local development. This file holds placeholders only: never put a real secret,
# key or production value in it. Secrets (LiveKit API secret, host and moderator keys, viewing keys,
# API tokens) come from the real environment of the deployment, never from a committed file.

# Set to exactly "production" to switch the Origin allowlist (see
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS below) to its strict production policy. Anything else
# (unset, "development", "test") gets the permissive-but-local dev
# policy. Leave as "development" (or unset) for local work.
NODE_ENV=development

# Port the WebSocket server listens on.
PORT=8787

# Host/interface to bind. 0.0.0.0 to accept connections from other devices on
# your LAN (e.g. testing from a phone); 127.0.0.1 to restrict to this machine.
HOST=127.0.0.1

# Stale-connection cleanup: a connection that hasn't sent any message
# (join/player_transform/heartbeat) in this many ms is closed and removed.
STALE_TIMEOUT_MS=30000

# Comma-separated list of allowed WebSocket Origins. This is a
# configuration safety check against hostile *websites* opening a
# WebSocket to this server — it is NOT an authentication mechanism (see
# src/origin.ts for the full reasoning).
#
# - NODE_ENV != production (including unset): these are added ON TOP OF
#   the built-in local-dev defaults (http://localhost:5174,
#   http://127.0.0.1:5174, plus :5173 used by the e2e tests — see
#   src/origin.ts), which is why the example
#   value below is redundant with those defaults but harmless.
# - NODE_ENV = production: the dev defaults are NOT included. The
#   allowlist is exactly what you put here — replace the example value
#   with your deployed web client's origin(s) (e.g.
#   https://game.example.com). No production hostname is
#   hardcoded anywhere in this repository — this is the only place it's
#   ever configured. If this is left empty while NODE_ENV=production,
#   the server refuses to start rather than run with zero allowed
#   browser Origins (a near-certain misconfiguration, not an intended
#   empty allowlist) — see src/index.ts.
#
# A browser connecting with an Origin not in the resolved list is
# rejected; a request with no Origin header at all (non-browser clients,
# e.g. this project's own test suite) is allowed either way, in both
# environments — see docs/protocols/multiplayer-protocol.md § Origin
# validation for why.
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5174,http://127.0.0.1:5174

# Serve the built web client from this server (one origin for the page, the WebSocket, voice tokens, the
# content gateway and the wallet bridge): the path of apps/web/dist. Unset: the page is served elsewhere
# (in development, by Vite).
# WEB_DIST=

# --- Voice (ADR-007) ----------------------------------------------------------
#
# Local development: leave these empty. The root `npm run dev`
# starts a local LiveKit (scripts/dev/livekit.mjs downloads livekit-server
# 1.13.8 once, verifies its checksum and caches it under
# node_modules/.cache/livekit) and runs this server with --local-livekit,
# which uses ws://127.0.0.1:7880 with the --dev keys (devkey / secret).
# SKIP_LOCAL_LIVEKIT=1 turns that off; LOCAL_LIVEKIT_PORT moves it. It never
# applies with NODE_ENV=production. See apps/web/README.md § Voice.
# SKIP_LOCAL_LIVEKIT=1
# LOCAL_LIVEKIT_PORT=7880
#
# Voice is OPTIONAL: if any of the three LIVEKIT_* variables below is
# unset (and the local development LiveKit isn't used), the /voice/token
# endpoint responds 503 {"error":"voice_unconfigured"} and the rest of the
# application (multiplayer, nickname, social) is completely unaffected —
# see src/voice/config.ts. There is no default/placeholder value here on
# purpose: an accidentally-real value must never be this file's problem,
# and a missing value should visibly disable the feature, not silently
# half-work. Setting all three uses YOUR LiveKit (npm run dev then starts
# no local one).
#
# LIVEKIT_API_KEY / LIVEKIT_API_SECRET: used ONLY server-side, to SIGN
# short-lived voice tokens (apps/server/src/voice/tokenHandler.ts) — they
# are never sent to a browser and never appear in the client bundle. For
# local development, run a self-hosted livekit-server in --dev mode,
# which prints a placeholder devkey/secret pair to its own console — see
# apps/server/README.md § Voice for the exact command. Do NOT
# put a real production secret in this file or in .env.
LIVEKIT_API_KEY=
LIVEKIT_API_SECRET=

# The ws(s):// URL BROWSERS use to reach your LiveKit server — this is
# not a secret, just an endpoint (matches VITE_VOICE_TOKEN_URL's target
# process in apps/web/.env.example, but this is LiveKit's own port, not
# the gameplay server's). For local dev with `livekit-server --dev`:
LIVEKIT_URL=ws://localhost:7880

# The single shared voice room of the public world — not a private-room
# system. Defaults to "public-world" if unset.
LIVEKIT_ROOM_NAME=public-world

# --- Community content gateway (ADR-009) --------------------------------------
#
# Optional: GitHub token used ONLY server-side by the community content
# gateway (src/content/) to raise GitHub API rate limits for repository
# stats. Read-only public data; never sent to clients. Leave unset to use
# unauthenticated requests (stats may then be unavailable when rate-limited;
# READMEs still load).
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Optional: the Watch Hall catalogue (channels, replay collections, recurring
# events, public calendars, one-off events and the panel credits) as a JSON file
# in the shape of src/content/watchCatalogTypes.ts. Unset: a deployment-provided
# catalogue file next to src/ when one exists (see src/content/watchCatalogFile.ts),
# else the built-in sample catalogue. A file that does not parse stops the server
# at start.
# WATCH_CATALOG_FILE=

# Optional: YouTube Data API v3 key used ONLY server-side by the Watch Hall
# catalogue (GET /content/watch*, src/content/watch.ts). It enables live /
# upcoming status, viewer counts and view counts for the allowlisted Zcash
# channels, through playlistItems.list and videos.list only (1 quota unit
# each; never search.list). It is never logged, never part of a cache key and
# never sent to clients. Leave unset to use the public Atom feeds plus the
# curated replay catalogue (no live status). Restrict the key to the YouTube
# Data API in the Google Cloud console.
# YOUTUBE_API_KEY=

# --- Watch Hall (ADR-014) -------------------------------------------------------
#
# WATCH_HALL_HOST_KEY: the secret that unlocks the Watch Hall host role
# (force-stop / hand over / lock the stage, give the floor, lower hands, set
# the card while idle). A player types it into the stage widget inside the
# hall; the server compares SHA-256 digests in constant time, allows 5
# attempts per session (there is deliberately no process-wide budget, which
# a griefer could keep empty to lock real hosts out — the key's strength is
# the brute-force bound), and keeps the role for that session only. It is
# never logged, echoed, persisted or sent to any client. Unset, empty,
# shorter than 24 or longer than 128 characters, or fewer than 10 distinct
# characters → host features are disabled (hall_host_auth answers
# host_disabled; the startup log says why, never the key). Generate one with
# `openssl rand -base64 32`. Do NOT put a real production key in this file
# or in a committed .env.
# WATCH_HALL_HOST_KEY=
#
# WATCH_HALL_MAX_TURN_MS: cap on one stage turn, in milliseconds. A turn that
# has lasted longer ends while the stage is unlocked, other players are
# queued and no host is in the hall. Values above 24 h are capped at 24 h.
# Unset or empty (default) → 60 minutes; 0 → no cap.
# WATCH_HALL_MAX_TURN_MS=1800000

# --- Moderation (ADR-019) -------------------------------------------------------
#
# MODERATOR_KEYS: comma-separated moderator secrets. A player types one into
# Profile → "Moderator sign-in" (or the Watch Hall's "Unlock host tools" — the
# same field takes both keys) and is a moderator for that session: Mute / Kick /
# Ban in any player's menu, the Moderation panel (reports, the log, active bans
# and mutes) and every Watch Hall host power. Each key follows the host key's
# rules (24–128 characters, at least 10 distinct); a weaker one is ignored (the
# startup log says how many, never a key). Compared as SHA-256 digests in
# constant time; 5 tries per session; never logged, echoed or stored. Unset: no
# moderators (reports are then refused with "no moderators set up").
# Generate one with `openssl rand -base64 32` (base64 has no commas).
# MODERATOR_KEYS=
#
# MAX_SESSIONS_PER_IP: concurrent game sockets per network (default 4), plus at
# most 10 new connections per minute per network. Counted by a keyed hash of
# the client address (HMAC with a random per-process key; the address itself is
# never stored or logged). 0 turns BOTH limits off — for local load tests and
# the e2e suite only (every client is 127.0.0.1), never a public server.
# MAX_SESSIONS_PER_IP=4
#
# TRUST_PROXY: comma-separated IP address(es) of your reverse proxy. Only a
# connection FROM one of them may name the client with X-Forwarded-For (its
# rightmost entry); from anyone else the header is ignored, so it can't be
# spoofed. Unset: the socket's peer address counts (correct without a proxy;
# behind one, every player would share the proxy's address). Behind a reverse
# proxy, set the proxy's fixed address here.
# TRUST_PROXY=
#
# LIVEKIT_API_URL: where the moderation tools reach LiveKit's RoomService to stop
# a publisher (canPublish:false when a host/moderator/vote ends a stage turn or
# an identity is lost; removal on kick or ban). Default: LIVEKIT_URL's host over
# http(s). Set it when the server reaches LiveKit on an internal address (e.g.
# http://livekit:7880 on a private container network).
# LIVEKIT_API_URL=

# --- Test chain: faucet and owned names (ADR-016) -------------------------------
#
# ZCASHD_RPC_URL / ZCASHD_RPC_USER / ZCASHD_RPC_PASS: the JSON-RPC endpoint of a
#   zcashd node on a regtest/test chain run by the deployment. Enables the test-coin
#   faucet (POST /zcash/faucet; FAUCET_ZEC per claim, default 1) and the zcashd
#   name registry. Unset: no faucet. Refused on main.
# ZCASHD_RPC_URL=
# ZCASHD_RPC_USER=
# ZCASHD_RPC_PASS=
# FAUCET_ZEC=1
#
# NAME_REGISTRY: off (default) | dev | zcashd | lightwalletd (see the mainnet section).
#   off    — no registry: ADR-015's honour mode (holders choose names with
#            set_nickname; free, not owned, nothing stored).
#   dev    — the fee flow with a FAKE scanner that confirms every reservation
#            after NAME_DEV_CONFIRM_MS (default 2000) without any payment. For
#            local development and the e2e suite only: the server refuses to
#            start with it when NODE_ENV=production. Names are kept in memory
#            unless NAME_REGISTRY_FILE is set.
#   zcashd — the real flow: a shielded payment with the registration memo to
#            NAME_REGISTRY_ADDRESS, seen through z_listreceivedbyaddress over
#            the faucet's zcashd RPC (ZCASHD_RPC_URL / _USER / _PASS). Without
#            an address or the RPC settings, registration is DISABLED (holders
#            keep Guest-style names; the startup log says why).
# NAME_REGISTRY_ADDRESS: the registry's Orchard unified address on the test
#   chain (uregtest1… / utest1…; mainnet is refused). Never logged. The
#   zcashd wallet that receives the fees must own it.
# NAME_FEE_ZEC: the confirmation fee (default 0.01, at most 0.1).
# NAME_REGISTRY_FILE: the JSON store (default ./data/names.json, relative to
#   the server's working directory). The server's only persistent data —
#   see docs/privacy/IDENTITY_THREAT_MODEL.md.
# NAME_REGISTRY=off
# NAME_DEV_CONFIRM_MS=2000
# NAME_REGISTRY_ADDRESS=
# NAME_FEE_ZEC=0.01
# NAME_REGISTRY_FILE=./data/names.json

# --- Network, payments and fees (ADR-018 — `main` means real ZEC) ---------------
#
# ZCASH_NETWORK: test (default) | main. On main the server
#   refuses to start with the faucet (ZCASHD_RPC_URL) or NAME_REGISTRY=zcashd|dev,
#   and LIGHTWALLETD_URL defaults to https://zec.rocks:443. The web client must be
#   built with the same VITE_ZCASH_NETWORK.
# LIGHTWALLETD_URL: the wallet bridge's upstream, one URL or an ordered comma-separated
#   list (at most 5) tried with failover, e.g. https://zec.rocks:443,https://eu.zec.rocks:443.
#   Default: https://zec.rocks:443 on main, https://testnet.zec.rocks:443 on test;
#   `off` disables the bridge (and with it every fee check).
# PAYMENT_CAP_ZEC: ADR-018 § 4 per-transaction cap on relayed payment requests
#   (default 0.01 on main, off on test; "off" lifts it).
# NAME_REGISTRY=lightwalletd: the name registry that works on mainnet — the paying client
#   reports its txid, the server decrypts that transaction with
#   NAME_REGISTRY_UFVK (or NAME_REGISTRY_UFVK_FILE). NAME_REGISTRY_ADDRESS must be
#   that key's own address (preferably the full u1… with Orchard, Sapling and
#   transparent receivers; a u1… with Sapling + transparent receivers or a zs1… also work).
#   On main it also needs NAME_REGISTRY_MAINNET_ACK=accepted (the operator's
#   explicit opt-in to charging real ZEC for names), else registration is
#   "disabled". NAME_MIN_CONF: confirmations a payment needs (default 1).
#   Keys: node scripts/tools/registry-keys.mjs (keep the seed offline; the server
#   only ever gets the viewing key).
# PAYMENT_FEE_ZEC: the transfer fee between players (ADR-018 § 6; default
#   0.00075 on main, off on test unless set). PAYMENT_FEE_ADDRESS and
#   PAYMENT_FEE_UFVK (or _FILE) default to the registry's; on main it needs
#   PAYMENT_FEE_MAINNET_ACK=accepted, else payments run without a fee.
#   PAYMENT_MIN_CONF: confirmations the fee needs (default 1).
# PAYMENT_FEE_USD / NAME_FEE_USD: optional approximate US-dollar labels of the
#   two fees (e.g. 1), shown as "≈ US$1" next to the ZEC amounts. Unset: ZEC only.
#   Re-check them with the price (the fees are fixed ZEC amounts).
# NU7_ACTIVATION_HEIGHT: optional, once NU7's height is announced — the fee check
#   then waits out NU7's longer transaction expiry (120 blocks) near and after it.
# BUILD_ID: the served client's build id when the client is hosted elsewhere
#   (default: WEB_DIST/build-id.txt) — the "Update ready — reload" prompt.
# CSP_MODE: with WEB_DIST, pages carry the full Content-Security-Policy
#   (connect-src: this origin, ALLOWED_ORIGINS and their ws(s) form, LIVEKIT_URL).
#   `minimal` keeps only frame-ancestors/object-src/base-uri — an escape hatch.
# HTTPS_PROXY / NO_PROXY: an outbound HTTP CONNECT proxy for the wallet bridge's
#   upstream connections, when the server has no direct internet access.
# CSP_MODE=
# ZCASH_NETWORK=test
# LIGHTWALLETD_URL=
# PAYMENT_CAP_ZEC=
# NAME_REGISTRY_UFVK=
# NAME_REGISTRY_MAINNET_ACK=
# NAME_MIN_CONF=1
# PAYMENT_FEE_ZEC=
# PAYMENT_FEE_ADDRESS=
# PAYMENT_FEE_UFVK=
# PAYMENT_FEE_MAINNET_ACK=
# PAYMENT_MIN_CONF=1
# PAYMENT_FEE_USD=
# NAME_FEE_USD=
# NU7_ACTIVATION_HEIGHT=
# BUILD_ID=
